<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Aprila and DNB concludes cooperation on offering credit lines to SMEs</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-12-16 12:57:39</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>With reference to notification from 2021-09-02 regarding a one-year pilot agreement with DNB, the cooperation is now concluded. The initiative to run tests and experiments to learn more about how to best serve small businesses and their financing needs ends this year.<br> <br>The offering will be removed from DNB’s web properties on 31 December, and the final date of the cooperation will be 21 February 2023 when Aprila no longer will onboard further customers via DNB.  <br><br>The learnings from the initiative have been satisfactory. However the financial impact is small for both Aprila and DNB. The initiative resulted in 139 credit line customers which originated from DNB, with a total lending balance in Aprila of NOK 15 million, corresponding to ~2% of Aprila’s total customer base and lending balance. <br><br>Aprila will continue to supply credit to the credit line customers that were sourced from DNB after the distribution agreement has ended. <br><br>“We have appreciated the cooperation we have had with DNB and their interest in Aprila’s automated data driven credit and will continue our journey to close the SME funding gap in Norway on our own and with our other excellent partners” says Halvor Lande, CEO of Aprila.<br><br>***<br><br>Contact person Aprila Bank:<br>Halvor S Lande<br>CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br><br>Contact person DNB:<br>Vibeke Lewin<br>EVP Communications DNB<br>+47 990 13 349<br>Vibeke.lewin@dnb.no<br><br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila Bank is a product and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is built to scale and is currently connected to around 150,000 SMEs through partnerships with leading business system providers.<br><br>=== About DNB ASA ===<br>DNB is Norway's largest financial services group and one of the largest in the Nordic region in terms of market capitalisation. The Group offers a full range of financial services, including loans, savings, advisory services, insurance and pension products for retail and corporate customers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Notification of trade</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-12-12 08:04:57</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Kvantia AS and Hafa Invest AS have respectively purchased 21,000 and 157,500 shares in Aprila Bank ASA on 9 December 2022. Hafa Invest AS is an investment company wholly owned by primary insider in Aprila Bank ASA, Hans Marius Falkanger. Mr. Falkanger also works as an investment professional in Kvantia AS. The shares were purchased at NOK 6.50 per share. After the purchase, Kvantia AS and its subsidiary Christiana Skibs AS, hold 2,626,398 shares in the company, equal to 4.25% of the share capital and Hafa Invest AS holds 269,471 shares in the company, equal to 0.44% of the share capital.</p></td>
</tr>
