<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Business update</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-11-07 14:41:11</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Visma agreements signed<br>Reference is made to the letter of intent between Visma Norge Holding AS and Aprila announced on 5 September 2022. On 31 October 2022, Aprila Bank signed two concurrent agreements with Visma:<br><br>1. An Asset Purchase Agreement (“APA”) to regulate the transfer of the business of Visma Finance AS to Aprila Bank. The acquisition price is agreed to be the purchase price of the outstanding, current claims of Visma Finance AS, but no more than NOK 2,000,000.<br><br>2. A Private Placement Agreement, where Visma has committed to subscribe for NOK 22.5 million in Aprila Bank at a price of NOK 7.50 per share. <br><br>Closing of the APA is expected to take place on 22 December 2022. Aprila plans to hold an extraordinary general meeting to resolve the private placement on the same date. In addition to the subscription from Visma, Aprila’s two largest shareholders, SES AS and Amesto Group AS, will subscribe for NOK ~7.5 million, providing Aprila with around NOK 30 million in new equity.<br><br>Strong growth and profitability improvements among Aprila customers<br>There is limited evidence of a deteriorating business environment among Aprila’s ~6,000 business customers. The average business customer increased their revenue by 9% from Q3 21 to Q3 22, and average net profit margin increased by 0.4% to 10.3%. The strongest growth was in the services and constructions industries, whereas real estate and ICT experienced declining revenues and profitability.<br><br>Loan loss provisions were higher than expected due to improvement in PD model<br>Aprila booked loan loss provisions (LLPs) according to IFRS 9 of NOK 11 million, resulting in total reported losses of 11.9 million vs. expected NOK 9 million. Realised losses in the quarter amounted to NOK 0.9 million. The bank decided to increase LLPs due to improvements in the bank’s machine learning PD models. The improved PD models will further improve Aprila’s ability to select customers and price credit and will thus lay the foundation for increased growth and profitability going forward.<br><br>Negative Q3 result of NOK 3.6 million, driven by elevated loan loss provisions<br>Total income in the quarter amounted to NOK 25.2 million, representing a growth of 87% YoY and 10% QoQ. The moderate QoQ growth was due to reduced spot factoring volumes and moderate customer demand in July and August.<br><br>Total expenses amounted to NOK 16.8 million in the quarter, up 9% compared to Q3 21. Cost/Income in Q3 was 67%, compared to 115% in Q3 21.<br><br>Despite the significant amount of loan loss provisions, net interest margin after losses(*) remained high at 10.6% in Q3. Going forward, Aprila expects net interest margin after losses to be around 15%.<br><br>Pre-tax operating profit for the quarter was negative NOK 3.6 million, compared to negative NOK 5.4 million for Q3 21.<br><br>Record number of new credit line customers onboarded in Q3<br>Aprila onboarded 489 credit line customers in Q3, a new quarterly record. At the end of the quarter Aprila had 3,241 credit line customers, with an average annualised gross income per customer of NOK 33k from interest rates and fees. <br><br>Aprila’s gross income from lending run-rate was NOK 130 million, up from NOK 114 million at the end of Q2 (+14%), and NOK 74 million at the end of Q3 21 (+75%).<br><br>The results will be presented in a webcast with CEO Halvor Lande and CFO Kjetil Barli on 14 November 2022 at 10:00 CET.<br><br>The presentation and subsequent Q&A session will be held in English and may be viewed live at https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations/webcast.<br><br>A recording of the presentation will be made available on https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations after the presentation.<br><br>About Aprila Bank<br>Aprila is a product- and technology company offering improved access to financing for businesses through innovative financial solutions. Aprila’s API-based technology platform supports both direct customer relationships as well as customer relationships established through partners. The bank commenced operations in April 2018.<br><br>Notes:<br>(*) Net interest margin after losses defined as net interest income plus net commissions and fees divided by net loans and annualised.<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br><br>Halvor S. Lande<br>CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br><br>Kjetil S. Barli<br>CFO<br>+47 908 42 016<br>kjetil@aprila.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
