</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Interim results Q1 2022</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-05-12 08:10:50</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila Bank delivered a pre-tax profit of NOK -5.3 million in the first quarter of 2022; its best quarterly result since the start of operations in Q2 2018. Total income amounted to NOK 17.9 million, an increase of 107% YoY. The result is supported by an all-time high number of new credit line customers. <br><br>Key figures at the end of the quarter:<br>- Gross loans amounted to NOK 438 million, an increase of 106% YoY<br>- Gross lending to credit line accounts amounted to NOK 377 million, an increase of 144% YoY <br>- 5,344 unique customers, an increase of 53% YoY<br>- 6,086 open customer accounts, an increase of 52% YoY<br><br>The report and presentation are available on the company’s website:<br>https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations<br><br>Aprila will present the results today at 10:00 CET.<br><br>A recording of the presentation will be made available on https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations after the presentation.<br><br>About Aprila Bank<br>Aprila is a product- and technology company offering improved access to financing for businesses through innovative financial solutions. Aprila’s API-based technology platform supports both direct customer relationships as well as customer relationships established through partners. The bank commenced operations in April 2018.<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br><br>Halvor S. Lande<br>CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no <br><br>or<br><br>Kjetil S. Barli<br>CFO<br>+47 908 42 016<br>kjetil@aprila.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Invitation to presentation of Q1 2022</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-05-05 17:00:20</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila Bank ASA reports the interim results for the first quarter on 12 May 2022. A presentation will be held as a meeting in Microsoft Teams.<br><br>Date: 12 May 2022<br>Time: 10:00 CET<br><br>Please register your attendance in advance by sending an e-mail to ir@aprila.no. The link to the meeting will be distributed when your attendance is registered.<br><br>The presentation will be available on the company's website:<br>https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations<br><br>Contact person at Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Kjetil Barli, CFO<br>+47 908 42 016<br>kjetil@aprila.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SpareBank1 SR-Bank and Aprila Bank to cooperate on offering credit to small businesses</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-05-05 08:59:29</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila is pleased to announce that an agreement has been signed with SpareBank 1 SR-Bank (“SR-Bank”) for the distribution of Aprila’s digital and automated Credit Line through SR-Bank channels.<br>SR-Bank and Aprila have a shared vision of helping small businesses succeed. Our common goal is to contribute to the creation of new jobs and the growth and success of small businesses and thereby the strengthening of local communities. <br>“With this credit line, companies will have money available for example to pay for variable expenses or for investments. Aprila has developed a simple application process, responds very quickly, and the funds are available shortly after signing” says Marianne Bakke, head of SMB and agriculture at SR-Bank. <br>“In Aprila, our goal is to help finance and build the jobs and the companies of the future. It corresponds very well with SR-Banks corporate promise to provide growth and development for small businesses. The cooperation with SR-Bank will mean that we can contribute to more jobs and more sustainable local communities. We can succeed in this even better together” says Halvor Lande, CEO of Aprila Bank.<br>“SMBs are the backbone of Norwegian business. When we say that we must add strength to these companies, it means that we must contribute to their success. Many of our smallest corporate customers are in need of credit, and with our partnership with Aprila we are now able to offer them an even broader array of credit products” adds Marianne Bakke.<br>Aprila's technology platform enables real-time credit scoring, pricing and credit decision based on machine learning technology. With transparent and understandable pricing and without pledge in assets, Aprila Credit Line can be offered even to start-ups.<br>The entire process of customer onboarding, credit application and credit decision won’t take more than around two minutes of the customers’ time. Aprila's technology is built on using “real time” data from multiple sources as well as traditional sources such as credit scoring, payment remarks etc. The models have been developed and trained over years to predict outcomes and price risk automatically. This high level of automation enables offering credit even to small companies.<br>***<br>Contact person Aprila Bank:<br>Halvor S Lande, CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>Halvor.lande@aprila.no<br><br>Contact person SpareBank 1 SR-Bank:<br>Marianne Bakke, Head of SMB and Agriculture<br>+ 47 958 93 388<br>Marianne.bakke@sr-bank.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Minutes of the ordinary general meeting</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-04-27 08:28:42</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>The ordinary general meeting in Aprila Bank ASA was held electronically on 26 April 2022 at 12.00 CET. All the proposed resolutions were passed.<br><br>The notice and the minutes from the meeting are available at https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations.<br><br>Contact person at Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Helge Benum, CRO<br>+47 911 02 637<br>helge.benum@aprila.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Exercise of warrants and notification of trades</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-04-13 14:42:18</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>On 18 April 2017, Aprila Bank ASA (the "Company") issued warrants to its early shareholders (the "Warrants"). The Warrants were issued with a duration of 5 years from 18 April 2017 and with a strike price of NOK 5.50 per new share. <br><br>Today, 13 April 2022, the following exercise of Warrants has taken place:<br>-	Amesto Group AS has exercised all Warrants owned by Amesto Group for 1,875,000 new shares<br>-	Amesto Group AS has acquired 360,000 shares through Disruptor AS' exercise of Warrants for 360,000 new shares<br>-	Equilibria ApS has exercised Warrants transferred from Primera AS for 1,650,000 new shares<br>-	SES AS has acquired 400,000 shares through Inchoate AS' exercise of Warrants for 400,000 new shares<br>-	Chri AS has acquired 180,000 shares through Disruptor AS' exercise of Warrants for 180,000 new shares<br>-	Primera AS has exercised Warrants for 100,000 new shares<br>-	Morten Goller has exercised Warrants for 62,500 new shares<br><br>In total Warrants for 4,627,500 new shares have been exercised at NOK 5.50 per share, providing Aprila Bank with a total of NOK 25,451,250 in new equity. <br><br>As set out above, certain Warrants were transferred or exercised in together with a sale of shares immediately before exercise. No Warrant holder has had any gain from the sale of the Warrants or the resulting shares, as all Warrants or rights to shares that have been transferred were transferred without other consideration to the holder than the obligation to exercise the warrants and provide equity to the Company.<br><br>After completion of the share issue, the primary insiders in the Company who exercised Warrants will have the following holding: <br>-	Arild Spandow, chairman of Aprila Bank and representing Amesto Group AS, will hold 9,568,374 shares, equal to 17.3% of the share capital<br>-	Bertel Steen, board member of Aprila Bank and representing SES AS, will hold 5,450,505 shares, equal to 9.9% of the share capital<br>-	Per Christian Goller, CGO of Aprila Bank and owner of Primera AS, will hold 1,786,500 shares, equal to 3.2% of the share capital.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Annual report and Pillar 3 report 2021</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-03-31 09:03:09</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>The company’s annual report for 2021 and the company’s Pillar 3 report for 2021 are now available at https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations.<br><br>Contact person at Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Kjetil Barli, CFO<br>+47 908 42 016<br>kjetil@aprila.no</p></td>
</tr>
