<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Aprila partners with the Visma company Presis Utleie AS on home rental platform</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-12-04 09:04:22</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Presis Utleie AS, a Visma company, has developed a digital platform for home rental and home rental administration. Through Presis Utleie, landlords can reduce their time spent on managing tenants while at the same time ensuring predictable income. Aprila will offer deposit accounts and invoice factoring through the platform.<br><br>The offering combines Presis’ digital home rental platform with Aprila’s seamless and digital financing offerings to create a complete tool for home rental administration, where Aprila’s invoice factoring offering will ensure that landlords get paid on time.<br><br>“Visma is committed to develop innovative new software solutions to digitize and transform the real estate industry, and we look forward to launching this new platform, and to further evolve our partnership with Aprila,” says Eivind Gundersen, Division Director Visma.<br><br>The platform is expected to be launched during Q1 21.<br><br>“We are excited to enter into this partnership with Presis Utleie and to establish a new distribution platform for our seamless and automated financing offerings. The solution builds on the technology behind Aprila’s spot factoring, and we are excited to develop a new channel for this product,” says Halvor Lande, CEO of Aprila.<br><br>***<br>Contact person Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Halvor S Lande<br>CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br><br>Contact person Presis Utleie AS:<br>Eivind Gundersen<br>Division Director Visma<br>+47 932 17 677<br><br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila is a product and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses and retail customers. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is connected to around 130,000 SMEs through partnership agreements with leading cloud-based ERP and accounting system providers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Notification of trade</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-11-20 08:21:37</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Knut Asbjørnsen, Head of Sales in Aprila, has on 19 November purchased 26,666 shares in Aprila Bank ASA. The shares were purchased at NOK 7.50 per share.<br><br>After the purchase Knut Asbjørnsen holds 129,369 shares in the company.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Zmarta to offer business loans from Aprila</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-11-13 08:11:57</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Zmarta partners with Aprila and launches the first aggregator channel for business loans in Norway.<br><br>Zmarta Group is a leading aggregator for financial and utility services in Scandinavia, with 1.2 million customers and a #1 market position in Norway, Sweden and Finland. Zmarta is owned by Bauer Media Group, one of the largest media houses in Europe. I Norway, Bauer Media owns and operates nine radio channels, including Radio Norge, Radio 1 and Radio Topp 40.<br><br>“For Aprila, this is a big opportunity to boost customer and lending growth. Zmarta has an impressive track record in attracting large volumes of loan applications on their marketplaces. I believe Aprila will do very well in competition with other lending providers on the platform, due to our automated credit decision engine, which will be able to offer loans immediately to a high proportion of small and medium sized business applicants. Zmarta’s move to start offering business loans in Norway will help grow the Norwegian SME lending market, and thereby improve access to credit for Norwegian SMEs, which is much needed,” says Halvor Lande, CEO of Aprila. <br><br>“We look forward to launch with Aprila in Norway, and to repeat the success we have had with business loans in Sweden and Finland,” says Gustav Berghog, CEO of Zmarta Group.<br><br>***<br>Contact person Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Halvor S Lande<br>CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br><br>Contact person Zmarta Group AB:<br>Marcus Tinusson<br>Commercial Director SME<br>+46 (0) 70 089 4701<br>marcus.tinusson@zmartagroup.com<br><br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila is a product and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses and retail customers. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is connected to around 130,000 SMEs through partnership agreements with leading cloud-based ERP and accounting system providers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Notification of trade</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-11-06 14:50:33</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Julia Paulsen, Head of Marketing & Digital Sales in Aprila, has on 6 November purchased 64,000 shares in Aprila Bank ASA. The shares were purchased at NOK 7.80 per share.<br><br>After the purchase Julia Paulsen holds 64,000 shares in the company.</p></td>
</tr>
