<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Interim results Q3 2020</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-11-06 09:06:19</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila will present the Q3 results today, 6 November 2020, at 10:00 CET.<br><br>The presentation will be held in Microsoft Teams and can be joined via this link: https://bit.ly/3oH34BO.<br><br>The report and presentation are available on the company’s website:<br><br>https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations<br><br>Contact person at Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Kjetil Barli, CFO<br>+47 908 42 016<br>kjetil@aprila.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Aprila partners with Axactor to offer digital factoring</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-11-05 08:07:48</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila partners with Axactor to offer digital factoring to medium sized businesses. The new offering will allow businesses with annual invoice volumes from NOK 20 million to NOK 5 billion to receive immediate and hassle-free payment for their invoices. The solution only requires a few days to set up for any business using any accounting system.<br><br>The offering combines Axactor’s technology platform, invoice distribution and collection services with Aprila’s platform for automated claim valuation and purchase to create a completely new offering:<br><br>- Full and immediate payment of invoices as soon as they are issued<br>- Significant reduction in load on customer services from invoice inquiries <br>- Automated booking of all transactions in the customer’s accounting system<br><br>This offering has three significant advantages over traditional factoring:<br><br>1.Immediate conversion of accounts receivables to cash. This allows for increased and more cost-effective operational leverage<br>2. Streamlined and reduced accounting effort, as opposed to traditional factoring that significantly increases accounting costs<br>3. Fully accelerated and predictable cash flow, instead of traditional factoring that creates a less predictable and only partially accelerated cash flow<br><br>Axactor Group is an industry challenger providing innovative, cost efficient and IT powered next-generation debt management solutions. The company has risen from a start-up to Europe’s top 10 in four years. Axactor performs debt purchases, debt collection and accounts receivables management as its main business activities and is currently operating in six markets; Spain, Norway, Germany, Italy, Sweden and Finland. Axactor is built on a passion for efficiency. Through its 'One Axactor' platform, efficiency is enabled through leading people, systems and funding.<br><br>“We have multiple requests from businesses that want us to provide immediate invoice payments. We believe that this solution will solve an unmet need in the market today and are excited about partnering up with Aprila on this,” says Stina Koren, Country Manager for Axactor Norway.<br><br>The total factoring market in Norway amounts to NOK 260 billion in financed invoices annually, and Aprila and Axactor hope to capture a significant share of this market together over time. <br><br>“For Aprila this is an important step to be able to provide attractive and relevant financial solutions for medium sized businesses in Norway, and eventually in other countries. The solution builds on the technology behind Aprila’s spot factoring product, which has been a big success for small businesses in Norway,” says Halvor Lande, CEO of Aprila.<br><br>***<br>Contact person Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Halvor S Lande<br>CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br><br>Contact person Axactor Norway AS:<br>Stina Koren<br>Country Manager<br>+47 922 62 652<br>stina.koren@axactor.com<br><br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila is a product and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses and retail customers. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is connected to around 130,000 SMEs through partnership agreements with leading cloud-based ERP and accounting system providers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Invitation to presentation of Q3 2020</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-10-30 08:46:36</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila Bank ASA reports the interim results for the third quarter on 6 November 2020. A presentation will be held as a meeting in Microsoft Teams.<br><br>Date: 6 November 2020<br>Time: 10:00 CET<br>Link: https://bit.ly/3oH34BO<br><br>Please register your attendance upfront by sending an e-mail to ir@aprila.no.<br><br>The presentation will be available on the company's website:<br>https://www.aprila.no/investor-relations<br><br>Contact person at Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Kjetil Barli, CFO<br>+47 908 42 016<br>kjetil@aprila.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Distribution agreement for new product</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-10-14 08:17:48</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila is pleased to announce that we have signed a distribution agreement with Fair Group AS for the integration of Aprila Deferred Payment in the Fair Distribution platform (“Fair Distribution”). Together the parties intend to offer deferred payment to Fair’s customers in the business-to-business segment. <br><br>Fair Distribution is an invoice distribution platform, which means that as a single point of delivery for outgoing invoices, the platform finds the best way to reach the recipient, whether electronically (eFaktura, AvtaleGiro, Vipps, digipost, email or EHF) or by mail. Fair distributes 20 million invoices annually in Norway on behalf of their customers. <br><br>Aprila Deferred Payment adds a “button” on the invoices distributed through the platform, enabling the recipient to choose delayed payment of the invoice (if qualified by Aprila). This new product fits well with Aprila’s focus on providing frictionless and integrated banking services to small and medium sized businesses in the interfaces they already use.<br><br>“By introducing the ability for a recipient of an invoice to pay later, while Aprila pays the issuer of the invoice on time, Aprila has added another convenient and accessible product to its SMB offering. We are proud to introduce this innovative product in cooperation with Fair, to a market which is underserved with financing options. We look forward to launching this new product during the next few months,” says Halvor S Lande, CEO of Aprila.<br><br>“Aprila Deferred Payment adds further value to our distribution platform and provides recipients of invoices with a completely new opportunity to finance their operations through delayed payments. We expect this new product to “grease the wheels” in the SMB sector, and look forward to offering this quick and innovative access to financing to invoice recipients,” says Christian Aandalen, CCO and co-founder of Fair Group AS.<br><br>Aprila will reach a new audience for SMB financing with this product and expects its deferred payments financing option to be introduced in several systems where invoices are generated going forward.<br><br>***<br><br>Contact person Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Halvor S Lande<br>CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br><br>Contact person Fair Group AS:<br>Christian Aandalen<br>CCO<br>+47 924 19 329<br>ca@fair.no<br><br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila is a product and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses and retail customers. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is connected to around 130,000 SMEs through partnership agreements with leading cloud-based ERP and accounting system providers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Operational and financial update Q3 2020</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-10-07 15:10:11</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila’s gross income from lending grew by 68% in the third quarter, to an all-time high of NOK 5.9 million.<br><br>Gross loans amounted to NOK 121 million at the end of the quarter, an increase of NOK 45m (+59%) compared to the end of Q2 2020. The credit line product launched in December 2019 accounted for 61% of gross loans at the end of the quarter.<br><br>Purchased amount in Q3 2020 amounted to an all-time high NOK 115 million, compared to NOK 80 million in Q2 2020. The 43% growth in purchased amount is a result of an increase in available invoicing volumes (invoiced amount), and a new decision engine for spot factoring launched on 5 September 2020. NOK 54 million (47%) of the purchased amount was purchased in September, surpassing the previous all-time high from October 2019 with a margin of NOK 13m (30%).<br><br>At the end of the third quarter, Aprila had 2,274 SME customers, an increase of net 462 customers (+25%) since the end of the second quarter of 2020. Fiken accounted for ~37% of the customers added in the quarter, followed by Visma eAccounting with ~32%, own channels with ~16%, Tripletex with 8% and other channels with ~6%.<br><br>The partnership with Visma.net Webfaktura announced on 25 September is proceeding as planned and launch is expected during Q4 2020.<br><br>Aprila will continue to develop its close partnership with Visma in order to jointly cover customers’ financial needs with financial products embedded in Visma’s online accounting systems, and Aprila will simultaneously increase its focus on own direct channels and other identified partner opportunities with a high potential. Aprila has today launched a new website designed for customer acquisition and will launch our first real marketing campaign next week.<br><br>Going forward Aprila will gradually become increasingly diverse in terms of products, distribution channels and partnerships, and thus less dependent on any single partnership.<br><br>Aprila expects the strong growth to continue.<br><br>Aprila’s Q3 presentation will be held on Friday 6 November 2020.<br><br>***<br>Contact person at Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Kjetil S. Barli, CFO<br>+47 908 42 016<br>kjetil@aprila.no<br><br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila is a product and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses and retail customers. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is connected to around 130,000 SMEs through partnership agreements with leading cloud-based ERP and accounting system providers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Visma to replace Aprila as spot factoring vendor in Visma-owned online accounting systems in Q2 2021</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-10-07 08:35:23</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila has been notified that Visma intends to replace Aprila’s spot factoring products in Tripletex and Visma eAccounting with its own solutions. This is expected to take place during Q2 2021.<br><br>Aprila will continue its close partnership with Visma as an API banking partner, delivering innovative financial solutions to Visma’s small and medium sized business customers.<br><br>We are very satisfied with our partnership with Aprila, and, although we now intend to replace Aprila as the vendor of spot factoring in our online accounting systems, Aprila will remain as our API banking partner,” says Eivind Gundersen, Division Director in Visma Commerce Solutions. <br><br>Spot factoring delivered to customers of Visma currently represents ~30% of Aprila’s gross loans. Spot factoring from customers of all Visma-owned accounting systems was expected to represent 25% of Aprila’s total income in 2021 and 15% of Aprila’s total income in the period 2021-2024.<br><br>“We appreciate that Visma has informed us about their plans several months ahead of their planned launch of Visma’s own products. This way, Aprila will, with a high degree of probability, have sufficient time to replace the lost income with new products and distribution partners. We have a long list of new endeavours that we could undertake, and we have shortlisted a very promising set of initiatives. Hence, I am confident that we will continue to deliver on the business plan,” says Halvor Lande, CEO of Aprila. <br><br>***<br>Contact person Aprila:<br>Halvor S Lande<br>CEO<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br>+47 924 32 305<br><br><br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila is a product- and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses and retail customers. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is connected to around 130,000 SMEs through partnership agreements with leading cloud-based ERP and accounting system providers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: New distribution agreement</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-09-25 08:51:29</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila is pleased to announce that we have signed a distribution agreement with Visma Software AS for the integration of Aprila Spot Factoring in the Visma.net Webfaktura invoicing system (“Webfaktura”).<br><br>Webfaktura is the online invoicing system for Visma Business - the most widely used ERP system in Norway.<br><br>Visma and Aprila expect spot factoring to be made available for Webfaktura users in Q4 2020. <br><br>Spot factoring enables businesses to sell and get paid for invoices as they are created, thus improving liquidity and removing friction.<br><br>Visma is an important distribution partner for Aprila in terms of reaching businesses directly and in a natural environment for financial services. <br><br>“We are very happy that Visma through Webfaktura now will provide the opportunity to reach underserved businesses efficiently and conveniently with financing when they may need it. Customers of Webfaktura will also enjoy the fact that there are no commitments to being a customer of Aprila; you only pay for the services you use. We look forward to offering improved access to liquidity to the Visma Busines community,” says Halvor Lande, CEO of Aprila Bank. <br><br>“With the launch of spot factoring in Webfaktura we make it easier than ever for our users to take control of their financial situation. We look forward to offering this quick and innovative access to financing from Aprila to our users,” says Kristian Vederhus Lien, Visma Software AS.<br><br><br>Contact person Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Halvor S Lande<br>CEO<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br>+47 924 32 305<br><br>Contact person Visma Software AS<br>Kristian Vederhus Lien<br>Head of Products and Business Models<br>kristian.lien@visma.com<br>+47 476 23 758<br><br>https://www.visma.no/regnskapsbyra/webfaktura/<br><br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila is a product- and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses and retail customers. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is connected to around 130,000 SMEs through partnership agreements with leading cloud-based ERP and accounting system providers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Aprila wins Mastercard's Lighthouse program – will continue to work together on improving payments and financial services for SMEs</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-09-02 08:23:39</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila was recently declared as the overall winner of Mastercard’s Lighthouse program. In this program, Mastercard selected 15 fintech scale-ups from the Nordic and Baltic regions to explore partnership opportunities with Mastercard and incumbent Nordic banks.<br> <br>As a result, Aprila is now invited to join Mastercard’s global fintech accelerator program which will open for co-operation with large global financial institutions.<br><br>Mastercard and Aprila will also continue the joint efforts to develop, launch and distribute digital financing and payment services for SMEs in Europe.<br><br>“We are impressed by the progress, energy and solutions that Aprila brought to the Lighthouse program. They are in the right market at the right time. SMEs account for more than 90% of companies in the Nordics, but they have been underserved for a long time due to historical difficulties of servicing them profitably at scale. Now, thanks to software automation, large data reserves, and tools like the ones Aprila is bringing to the market, it is finally time for SMEs to get the attention they deserve. We look forward to serve more SMEs through our ongoing partnership efforts with Aprila,” says Mats Taraldsson, Head of Digital Development and Fintech Engagement in Mastercard Nordics and Baltics.<br><br>“We look forward to continue our efforts with Aprila to develop digital credit and account-based payment services for SMEs. This is an important opportunity for Nets Centurion to improve ease of doing business for SMEs in Nordics and beyond,“ says Anna-Karin Østlie, Head of Payments Norway in Nets Centurion, which was recently acquired by Mastercard.<br><br>15 companies from the Nordic and Baltic region took part in Mastercard’s Lighthouse Program 2020 Spring Edition. The winners, selected for their team strength, product innovation, execution feasibility and partnership potential, were announced during Latitude 59.  Aprila was declared the overall winner.<br><br>“We are humbled and inspired to have been picked as the winner among such an impressive class of fintech scale-ups. We look forward to continue working with Mastercard and Lighthouse partners to reinvent banking and bring superpowers to small businesses,” says Halvor Lande, CEO of Aprila.<br><br>***<br>Contact person at Aprila Bank ASA:<br>Halvor Lande, CEO<br>+47 924 32 305<br>halvor.lande@aprila.no<br><br>***<br>=== About Aprila Bank ASA ===<br>Aprila is a product- and technology company offering innovative financial solutions to small and medium sized businesses and retail customers. Aprila’s API-based technology platform is connected to around 130,000 SMEs through partnership agreements with leading cloud-based ERP and accounting system providers.<br><br>***</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
