<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: New distribution agreement</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2019-07-09 08:52:45</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aprila Bank is pleased to announce that we have signed a major new distribution agreement with Visma Mamut AS for the distribution of Aprila Invoice Sales through Visma eAccounting. <br><br>Visma and Aprila expect the spot financing product for smaller businesses to be made available for customers in the system in Q4 2019. With its 120,000 customers in the Nordics, of which 40,000 in Norway, Visma eAccounting is the largest cloud accounting system for micro- and small-sized businesses in Norway.<br><br>“We have been very fortunate to be granted the opportunity to establish and maintain a close partnership with Visma, which commenced with the integration of Aprila in the Visma-owned cloud accounting system Tripletex in April 2018. Visma was impressively bold to be the first to integrate bank financing inside a cloud accounting system. The results have been very good, and the positive impact on customers, Visma and Aprila is underlined when Visma now signs up a second system for integration with Aprila Bank” says Per Christian Goller, CEO of Aprila Bank.  <br><br>“We look forward to being able to offer immediate financing to our customers inside Visma eAccounting. We see this as a natural step forward in the bundling of services in a natural environment for the micro- and small-sized businesses” says Kenneth Løvold, CEO of Visma Mamut AS. <br><br>For more information, please contact:<br><br>Per Christian Goller, CEO Aprila Bank ASA<br>pcg@aprila.no<br>+47 404 01 444<br><br>https://aprila.no/om-aprila<br><br>Kenneth Løvold , CEO Visma Mamut AS<br>kenneth.lovold@visma.com<br>+47 997 07 670<br><br>https://www.visma.no/eaccounting/</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Aprila Bank ASA: Change of CEO</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2019-06-04 18:33:25</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Halvor Sannes Lande will take up the position as CEO of Aprila from August 1st 2019. Lande comes from the position as Executive Vice President for IT transformation at DNB.<br><br>The process of finding a new CEO was initiated by founder and current CEO Per Christian Goller and co-founder and Chairman Arild Spandow in December 2018.<br><br>Lande has an MSc in Mathematics from UiO and was formerly the founder and CEO of Risklab for 9 years, which developed risk tools for fund managers in Europe. After this he was with McKinsey & Company for 8 years before joining DNB in 2016. <br><br>«Aprila is more than a bank. We have an ambitious mission and want to be important for businesses in the countries we enter into. I am impressed by what Aprila is trying to create, and I have never previously seen a start-up delivering on its original business plan for as long as Aprila. It is still early days, and the potential for Aprila is enormous. And it will have a positive impact on the world, which is important to me” says Halvor Lande.<br><br>«I am very happy to welcome Halvor on board. He is fully aligned with what we want to achieve and is a great capacity. I look forward to taking up a role where I can focus on the growth and development of the bank» says Goller.<br><br>«We are now rigging for volume and expansion, and Halvor is a perfect match for us” says Spandow.<br><br>Landes current employer, DNB, is positive to new and good digital solutions for the SMB market:<br><br>«We have the same goal, and we have a good dialogue with Aprila. Learning and sharing between small and large players is good for all parties. We wish Lande good luck in his new role» says Director of Information, Even Westerveld in DNB.<br><br>For more information, please contact:<br><br>Halvor Lande, CEO in Aprila from August 1st 2019<br>Mail: halvor.lande@gmail.com<br>Mobile: +47 924 32 305<br><br>Even Westerveld, Director of Information, DNB<br>Even.Westerveld@dnb.no<br>Mobile: +47 400 16 744<br><br>CEO in Amesto and chairman Aprila Bank<br>Mail: arild.spandow@amesto.no<br>Mobile: +47 930 97 820<br><br>Aprila-founder and current CEO<br>Per Christian Goller<br>Mail: pcg@aprila.no<br>Mobile: +47 404 01 444<br><br>https://www.aprila.no/om-aprila</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
